cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Accessible Slides: vision-science checks for slides, posters and figures"
abstract: >-
  A coding-agent skill that audits presentations, conference posters and
  scientific figures for readers with vision loss. Checks colour-vision
  deficiency using dichromat simulation and CIEDE2000 separability, contrast
  against projection-adjusted thresholds, and text size derived from room
  geometry rather than rules of thumb.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cui
    given-names: Eric
    affiliation: >-
      Rotman Research Institute, Baycrest Academy for Research and Education;
      Department of Psychology, University of Toronto
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4307-589X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/moecui22/accessible-slides"
url: "https://github.com/moecui22/accessible-slides"
license: MIT
